/-!
# KFV §8: Lemma 16 forward and opposite as IL programs (paper layout)

* `fwdP Rc n = Rc (n-1); …; Rc 0` and `oppP Rc n = Rc 0; …; Rc (n-1)`;
  `fwd_ok` / `opp_ok`: by induction on the rounds, they compute `runDown F n` / the `foldl` of
  the rounds (`procQc` / `procQIc` of `KFV1Coef`).
* `layerCode h`: prefix rounds `h < b` by `p14Leaf` with one-bit chunks (`dK` row: individual
  kernels), the top round by `topCode`, chunk rounds by any Proposition 14 code `Cch h`
  (in the merged table: `KFM.prop14Ph_kTable`, packaged by `layerOK_chunk`).
* `fwdRound h = layerCode h ; J_E` (exponent table `trips … h` and `twC`),
  `oppRound h = J_{-E} ; layerCode h` (table `negTr (2r) (trips … h)`).
* **`lemma16_fwd_IL`**: `fwdP fwdRound ℓ` computes `procQc p (paperLayout) ℓ (partAxes al)
  (paperSel) ℓ`, i.e. (`co_procQ`) the coefficients of `GlueError.procQ`, the computed forward
  procedure of Lemma 16 / `GlueProp18`;
  **`lemma16_opp_IL`**: `oppP oppRound ℓ` computes `procQIc …` (`co_procQI`: `GlueProp18.procQI`).
  Cost: the sum of the round costs `layerCost h + cTab + cTw`.
-/

