-- Source module: Solutions.KFMRep
/-!
# KFM: arrays as lists and as box functions

The machine holds the arrays of the chain as row-major lists of Gaussian integers (numerators
at scale `2^p`); `LineNeed`/`ChirpNeedR` relate them to box functions by `RepPad`/`RepFull`.
Here the box function of a list is made explicit, so every list the machine produces names its
function:

* `kL K`: the coordinates of a box point as a list; `boxIx` is `decode` (`digL_decode`).
* **`funF p t zs`** (full `t`-box) and **`funP p s t zs`** (the `s`-box read out of the padded
  `t`-box): `toC (zs[enc K]) / 2^p`.
* **`repFull_iff`**, **`repPad_iff`**: a list represents exactly its own function (so the function
  a call returns is determined by the returned list).
* `grid_funF`, `grid_funP`: these functions are on the grid of `Q_p`.
* Pointwise list maps: **`RepPad.smul`** (`g z = c·z`, e.g. `× 2^γ`), **`RepPad.conj`**,
  **`RepPad.gmul`** (`zipWith (gmulT p)` is `Q_p(u · v)`).
-/

